/-
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K4/Law/ExchangeOwnAt.lean: CONDITIONAL: on the library's hypothesis h
on the public files and on every hypothesis named. THE FULL SIZE ALONE.

What is here. The thread's debt `ExchangeAtS` at the own item of the member of the feed-forward
layers' own rounds (sub-protocol K4), at the thread with the library's own values (`lettersHead`,
Honest/Thread/FirstHead.lean): `k4_exchange_of_ties` (Law/ExchangeOfTies.lean) AT THE LOT's OWN
READER OF THE TOKENS `k4Tokens` (Honest/K4/Part.lean), AT THE TEXT `k4LookAt` (Honest/K4/Look.lean)
FOR WHAT THE LOOKUP HAS SAMPLED, AND AT THE MEMBER's OWN PUBLIC DATA `k4PubAt` (Law/DearTop.lean),
with six of its hypotheses had from statements of other files: hQ (`k4Pub_head`,
Law/FrontCount.lean) · hx (`layAt_laid`, Law/W/LayAtHead.lean) · hL (`k4LookAt_head`,
Law/LookAtHead.lean) · hiW (`hiW_of_index`, Law/W/IndexHiW.lean) · hW (`layersTie_thr`,
Law/W/LayersOfIndex.lean) · hTokP (`hTokP_of_fine`, Law/W/TokOfFine.lean). In their stead stand
three clauses under the thread's parameter Vd, on the thread's own input: hI, hVd, hW4. Nothing new
is shown: one call. Its worth: Lean holds the six ends against the six binders.

  `k4_exchange_own_at`   **`ExchangeAtS T Said k (Item.formsT m 3 "own")`.**

Not shown here. b1, THE LOOKUP's OWN SENTENCE, WHICH HOLDS ALL THE CONTENT THAT IS LEFT OF THE
BATCHED SUMCHECK's OWN CLAIM, IS MOVED, NOT SHOWN: Law/ExchangeOfTies.lean's head says how: it is
had out of a clause of `ThrS`, the sentence of the thread's open item on the keys' worth, which is
owed behind the member of the lookup on the calls; what the public item `.left m` says beside its
test is spent likewise. SO THE CONCLUSION SPEAKS ONLY WHERE A THREAD STANDS THAT HOLDS THESE
ALREADY. WHAT STAYS, BY NAME. hI (`K4IndexIs`, Law/IndexIs.lean), under Vd: the Script's cells and
the honest side's reader of the weights are one index's matrix, at every row and column: it defines
a hypothesis; `indexIsAt_member` (Law/IndexIsAt.lean) has a member of its form without a script; of
it together with the other hypotheses no example is known to us; its head says what an input must be
for it to hold: its reader answers with the index's own matrix, so with 0 outside the table; the
type of an input does not give that; IT ASKS MORE THAN hiW AND hW SPEND. hVd, under Vd: the
verifier's tests on the request's words accept (the body of `reqFine`, Law/TokensSeat.lean, written
out). hW4, under Vd: the request file is whole words; `whole_of_okBy` (Law/W/WholeWords.lean) has it
where the description's own test on the instance accepts (`okStart`): the frame's statements on a
whole file take that as a premise (Honest/Thread/FileYes.lean); its `ready` does not call the test.
half, fits: on the prover's list of halves and on a public test, at these three letters:
`half_atPure_at` (Law/HalfAtPureBy.lean) and `fits_lookAt_tokens` (Law/ExchangeOwnBy.lean) have them
at the maker's prover; Lh: `laid_at` (Law/LaidAtGroup.lean) has it under h. hRdIs, Lh, hb₀, hKp,
hMask, hc: each is one of `k4_exchange_tenth`'s (Law/ExchangeTenth.lean), at these letters; its head
says of each what it asks. hc (`CellIsList`, Law/W/CellsTieOf.lean): the honest cells against the
list that the library's reader makes of the witness; it forces that list's images to stand still
inside the sizes: `cellIsList_thr` (Law/W/CellsStill.lean) has that from the same sentence at what
was heard, and Law/ExchangeOwnStill.lean asks it so. WHETHER ALL THE HYPOTHESES CAN STAND TOGETHER
AT AN HONEST SCRIPT HAS NOT BEEN TESTED: of h together with hRdIs, Lh, half, fits, hb₀, hKp, hMask,
hc, hI, hVd and hW4 no example is known to us, and nothing here was evaluated. THAT THE THREAD HOLDS
AT ANY RUN, OR THAT ANY STEP OF THE MEMBER ACCEPTS: the conclusion speaks only where `ThrS` stands
and a step accepts; where none does, it holds emptily. NOT COMPLETENESS. h: the library's hypothesis
`P5J.AtMgA` (Johnson/P5J/MgAtAll.lean). The side library AtFullSide proves, with no hypothesis, that
h has a member at one place (AtFullSide.Top.headMember_zFull, AtFullSide/Top/HeadMemberAtFull.lean,
whose own Limits say what it is worth). Every limit of the heads of Law/ExchangeOfTies.lean and
Law/ExchangeTenth.lean holds here: the arrow on `Behind`, the clauses of the thread that are spent,
the statements under Johnson/Goal/ on which they rest; the six statements that are called rest on
more of these: their heads name them. Beneath `k4LookAt_head` stand comparisons by Lean's own kernel
that no independent checker has replayed (Law/LookAtFill.lean, Law/ElevenHead.lean). No test that
can fail stands beside it. THE FULL SIZE ALONE, and the format's second hash function alone
(`OnBytes.secondHashFunction`). Nothing on soundness or on any other property. No property is claimed.
WHAT THIS FILE's IMPORTS REACH, by a program's walk from import to import that stops, unopened, at
every module under Johnson/Goal/, Johnson/D/, Johnson/Bridge/ or ThirdParty/, at every module whose
name begins Cb.Bridge, and at the names RecCompile.Honest…, RecCompile.Both… and RecCompile.PassH…:
it stopped at 81 modules under Johnson/Goal/, at 7 under Johnson/Bridge/ and at 1 that begins
Cb.Bridge; it saw 46 modules whose names hold RecCompile, none under Johnson/D/ or ThirdParty/ and
none of the three names. What lies behind the 89 is not counted: all the numbers are floors. It
imports files of the frame's authors and of the authors of the kind "lookup" (through
Law/ExchangeOfTies.lean and Law/LookAtHead.lean). A LAW, NOT A PART: no file that defines a part of
the proof file's description may import this one.
-/
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.ExchangeOfTies
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.LookAtHead
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.FrontCount
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.W.IndexHiW
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.W.LayersOfIndex
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.W.TokOfFine
import Johnson.Desc.ProofFile.Honest.K4.Law.W.LayAtHead

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

/- no default table of scales is in sight: a statement that reads a table says which -/
attribute [-instance] Inst.Model.Scl.ref

namespace ProofFile.Honest.K4.W
open OnBytes OnBytes.Model
open OnBytes.Desc.First.K4 (Par)
open OnBytes.Desc.First.K4.Honest
open OnBytes.Maker (WholeD)
open VerifiableInference.Desc (Place Chain Strs Block First.S)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.First (Item)
open VerifiableInference.Desc.Sound (MsgT seatTab)
open P5J (AtMgA CellsM TS)
open ProofFile.Honest.FirstThread (Script WtF lettersHead)
open ProofFile.Honest.K4.SeatedHead (LaidK4)
open OnBytes.Road.K4 (k4PlaceAt)

variable {Z : VerifierAndGoals.PublicFiles} {D : WholeD} {r : LPFD.Full.RunPF} {Zp : ProofFile.Pub} {Np : H2U.Places4}
  {cF : Chain TS ProofFile.Cl} {xh : VerifiableInference.Desc.First.Look.Place}
  (h : AtMgA OnBytes.secondHashFunction Z D r Zp Np cF xh) {Bk : ProverCoinCounts} {W₀ Rc Ky Tr X₀ X' : Type}
  (H : Prover W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Ky Tr X₀ X')
  (Q : Script Bk (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) (CellsM OnBytes.Flat.numsFull) P5J.At.Tok MsgT)
  (test : Nat → TS → Option String) (carryX : Nat → ProofFile.InstPub × TS → Strs → WtF → Prop)
  (item n₁ n₂ b₀ : Nat) (Vd : Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr → Prop)
  (Rd : Nat → Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr → TS → Prop) (Kp : Place → TS → TS → Prop)
  (w₁ : Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr)

/-- CONDITIONAL: on every hypothesis named; the head lists them. **THE EXCHANGE AT THE MEMBER's OWN
ITEM, AT THE LOT's OWN READER OF THE TOKENS, THE TEXT `k4LookAt` AND THE MEMBER's OWN PUBLIC DATA.**
ν, st, R: the parameters of the frame's list `csHead`. -/
theorem k4_exchange_own_at
    (ν : Nat) (st : Nat → TS → Prop) (R : Nat → Option Forest.Heard → Prop)
    (hRdIs : Rd = ridersOf (csHead ν st R))
    (Said : Nat → Coins Bk → Mid (Local W₀ Rc ProofFile.Inst Tr) X' → Prop) {k m g : ℕ}
    {x : Bool × Par} {blk₀ : Block TS ProofFile.Cl} (Lh : LaidK4 Zp cF k m g x blk₀)
    {cells : Tr → Cells} {weights : W₀ → Weights}
    (half : H.first.find? (fun z => z.place == IM.k4Place g) =
      some (k4Half cells weights k4Tokens k4LookAt (k4PubAt cF k x)))
    (fits : ∀ fr, drawsFit (declsTo cF.blocksInOrder k) fr = true → Vd w₁ →
      k4Fits (k4PubAt cF k x) (k4LookAt (k4PubAt cF k x) fr) (k4Tokens w₁.x) = true)
    (hb₀ : b₀ ≠ k + 1) (hKp : ∀ s s', K4KeepsM s s' → Kp (k4PlaceAt g) s s')
    (hMask : ∀ c s mm E,
      ThrS (lettersHead h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁).thread Said k c s mm E →
      K4MaskTieAt (lettersHead h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁).thread cells weights
        k4Tokens k4LookAt (k4PubAt cF k x) (h.𝔇.N.sent m 0) (seatTab h.𝔇.cs h.𝔇.arr h.𝔇.ms) c s mm)
    (hc : ∀ c s mm E,
      ThrS (lettersHead h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁).thread Said k c s mm E →
      ∀ d, CellIsList (k4PubAt cF k x)
        (k4Wit (k4PubAt cF k x) cells weights k4Tokens (k4LookAt (k4PubAt cF k x)) mm.st.input)
        ((h.𝔇.H.hid (Q.wit c mm.st.input (mm.st.heard ++ d))).MG g) x.2.hp.tl)
    (hI : Vd w₁ → K4IndexIs Q weights w₁)
    (hVd : Vd w₁ →
      (Zp.s₀.withReq (Verify.words32 w₁.x.pub.request)).reqOk Zp.p.X.T Zp.p.X.P.h.V = true)
    (hW4 : Vd w₁ → w₁.x.pub.request.size % 4 = 0) :
    ExchangeAtS (lettersHead h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁).thread Said k
      (Item.formsT m 3 "own") := by
  obtain ⟨xl, hx, -⟩ := layAt_laid h Lh
  exact k4_exchange_of_ties h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁ ν st R hRdIs Said Lh
    (k4Pub_head h Lh) half fits hb₀ hKp hx hMask (fun ξ => (k4LookAt_head h Lh ξ).2) hc
    (hiW_of_index h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁ Said k hI g)
    (hTokP_of_fine h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁ Said Lh hVd hW4)
    (fun _ _ _ _ hT =>
      layersTie_thr h H Q test carryX item n₁ n₂ b₀ Vd Rd Kp w₁ hI hT.1 xl x.2.hp.tl g)

end ProofFile.Honest.K4.W

#print axioms ProofFile.Honest.K4.W.k4_exchange_own_at
